Certainly! Below is a JavaScript function that takes a number as input and returns an array of all its factors:

```javascript
function getFactors(num) {
    let factors = [];
    for (let i = 1; i <= num; i++) {
        if (num % i === 0) {
            factors.push(i);
        }
    }
    return factors;
}
```

You can use this function to find the factors of any positive integer. For example, `getFactors(12)` will return `[1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12]`.
